Nilanjan

Thanks for your table of results. You have three species for which you have density estimates from both methods. The striking feature of your findings is a fairly small number of detections. For nilgai and chousingha, the coefficients of variation (CV) are nearly 50% for both methods. Although the point estimates are different, examining the confidence intervals fails to show statistical differences in estimates between the two methods.

For the sambar, the number of detections was larger and the CVs were somewhat reduced (nearer to 30-35%), yet statistical differences do not exist. The comparison of methods doesn't provide reliable evidence that would permit choosing a method going forward.

