> Sorry - thinking a bit more, for the parameter alpha taking values slightly above 1, the pdf is neither zero nor a maximum, so you may find it works for you. The problem then is how you deal with g(0). Perhaps simplest is to assume g(y)=0 at the y value where your fitted function is a maximum. I don’t think that adopting a g(0) from elsewhere is a good strategy - I would expect estimation to be sensitive to your choice of model for the pdf.
