> > >
> > > I'll definitely give gamma a try and see what happens. Assuming it seems to work, I guess a subsequent issue is how to assess its performance vs. a traditional left-truncated hr or hn function. The data used to fit the models won't be the same, so they can't be compared by AIC. Maybe perform a chi-squared test on the range of data that are common to both detection functions? Any other ideas?
> > >
